AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00001853> "Obsoleted because ambiguous name has caused much misuse. This term referred to the dorsal wing of the pharyngeal sclerite - but as this was only clear from its synonyms and part relations, it has frequently been used to refer to the ventral surface/layer of the wing blade. There are now 2 replacement terms: one referring to the ventral wing of the pharyngeal sclerite and the other to the dorsal surface of the wing (For IDs, see consider statements associated with this obsolete term).")
