AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00001866> "Bodenstein, 1950, uses the term pharynx to refer to the entire anterior portion of the larval foregut, which in this ontology is divided into the atrium (anterior) and pharynx (posterior).")
