AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0045366") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0089570") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> "One of 3 dorso-laterally located sensilla of the terminal organ.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> "dorso-lateral group of to sensillum")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> "FBbt:00002706")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002706> "Jurgens et al. (1986), explain that the DLP and DMP are considered to be of different origins to the other 7 papillae of the terminal organ/MxSO because their axons do not join the maxillary nerve and they are found in different locations in certain homeotic mutants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0074007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0075072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0089570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0201176") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> "External compound sense organ of the antenno-maxillary complex of the larval head, located amongst the cirri. It contains three 'knob-like' sensilla, one bi-dendritic and two mono-dendritic. Neurons of the ventral organ connect with the larval maxillary nerve and terminate in area 2 of the subesophageal ganglion.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> "vo")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> "FBbt:00002707")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt#cur>)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002707> "Evidence for maxillary segment origin comes from Schmidt-Ott et al., 1994. There is some disagreement about the number of sensilla in the ventral organ: Campos-Ortega and Hartenstein, 1997, mention only 3 - one with two neurons and the other two with one each; Singh and Singh, 1984, provide evidence for 5 sensilla, 4 innervated by one neuron, the other by four neurons. This ontology follows Singh and Singh, 1984.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002708> "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00002708> "V")
