AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00004213> "The name photoreceptor cell R1 is occasionally, mistakenly assumed to refer to any Rh1 (ninaE) expressing photoreceptor cell. This is incorrect. This term only refers to a type of adult eye photoreceptor cell. The name is based simply on the position of the rhabdomere within each ommatidium - see figure 4 in Wolff and Ready, 1993 (FBrf0064798).")
