AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007281> "Colomb et al., (2007) report that labral nerve projections pass through area 2 and into area 1 of the subesophageal ganglion. In the majority of cases they then target the contralateral area 2. An exception to this is one epiphysis fiber (which labels with Gr2a-Gal4) which targets inside area 4.")
