AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007427> "Following the proposals of BrainName, the posterior optic commissure is so called (rather than the posterior optic tract) because it connects both hemispheres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0193849") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00007428> "Neuron of the period-expressing LNv cluster, with a small cell body and generally located more dorsally than the l-LNv neurons (Helfrich-Forster, 1998). There are 5 cells present in each cluster, all except one of which express Pdf (FBgn0023178).")
