AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0111409") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0144836") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00011929> "Mushroom body neuroblasts continue to supply increasing numbers of Kenyon cells through the larval stages. The axons of these neurons follow the tracts laid down during embryonic development. Which tracts they contribute to varies depending on the stage of development: from first instar to third instar stage 1, they contribute to the gamma lobe; during third instar stage 2 and puparium formation each axon bifurcates and contributes to the alpha' and beta' lobes (during the pupal stage they contribute to the alpha and beta lobes).")
