AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100332> "Whilst Ito et al., (FBC:BrainName) appear to consider the adult recurrent nerve as extending from the frontal ganglion to the foregut, Rajashekhar and Singh (1994) consider the recurrent nerve to consist of the nerve tract extending from the frontal ganglion only to the point where the pharyngeal nerve and stomodeal nerve separate. We adopt the latter definition.")
