AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100532> "Bayraktar et al., 2010, show that type I neuroblasts can be differentiated from type II neuroblasts by being Deadpan-, Prospero- and Asense-positive.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0204899") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0207387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0209927") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18284664") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "Neuroblast that asymmetrically divides to produce a large daughter neuroblast cell and a smaller secondary neuroblast (also called a transit-amplifying GMC) that can generate up to ten daughter neurons (Boone and Doe, 2008).")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "sr544")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "2011-06-06T02:54:10Z")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "transiently amplifying neuroblast")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "transit amplifying neuroblast")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "fly_anatomy.ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "TA neuroblast")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "FBbt:00100533")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100533> "Bayraktar et al., 2010, show that type II neuroblasts can be differentiated from type I neuroblasts by being Deadpan-positive, but Prospero- and Asense-negative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "FlyBase:FBrf0204880") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FBbt_00100534> "A dMP2 neuron that expresses ILP7. All dMP2 neurons that survive in the larva (those in A6-9) are of this type. There are two per segment. All project to the hindgut. These projections have ILP7 positive swellings associated with circular visceral muscle. Their terminals are also sites of ILP7 localization.")
